  "supported_interpretations": [
    "The frozen fresh-parent/2000-update MPPI benchmark cannot identify walking prediction and has insufficient declared motion variation. This is an identification failure of the version, not a protected comparison in which all scores lost to MSE.",
    "Teacher source affects observed student outcomes under matched incoming packages, tapes and update counts, but source bundles different states, targets and trajectory structure; this contrast does not identify which feature caused the difference.",
    "The reference result demonstrates occasional learning of walking with width128 and2000updates; it does not prove capacity is sufficient for all MPPI targets or establish reliable individual competence.",
    "The observed MPPI action variation motivates treating residuals cautiously; it does not prove action averaging, smoothing, memory deletion or transport invariance is safe."
  ],
  "unresolved": [
    "Whether any pre-update candidate predicts a genuinely useful MPPI learning update better than MSE.",
    "How much teacher memory/randomness, coverage, action consequences, trajectory structure, finite fitting or policy capacity caused the transfer gap.",
    "Whether learned incoming packages create useful MPPI learning-outcome variation, or merely retain pre-existing walking or regress under new supervision.",
    "Whether any change improves a next standalone child while preserving teachers over multiple acquisition-learning rounds."
  ]
